{"id":"ltc-related-payments-sf-early","title":"San Francisco nursing homes: related-party transactions, 2015 to 2025 (the earlier years added)","question":"What did San Francisco nursing homes report paying related companies before 2019, and in 2020 and 2021?","finding":"San Francisco skilled-nursing homes listed related-party transactions of $25.6 million in 2015, $23.1 million in 2016, $20.5 million in 2017, $12.4 million in 2018, $12.6 million in 2019, $24.7 million in 2020, $17.4 million in 2021, $20.7 million in 2022, $13.6 million in 2023, $13.0 million in 2024, $19.0 million in 2025. Across all eleven years, 25 home-years show a loss smaller than what the home paid related parties; 19 of them are in the years added here ($48.1 million paid in those years): California Convalescent Hospital 2017 (loss $101,536, paid $144,092); Central Gardens 2015 (loss $599,304, paid $617,971); Central Gardens 2016 (loss $3,486, paid $392,371); Central Gardens 2017 (loss $108,180, paid $317,371); Central Gardens 2018 (loss $399,491, paid $694,912); City View Post Acute 2020 (loss $2.2 million, paid $5.1 million); City View Post Acute 2021 (loss $3.2 million, paid $4.9 million); Kindred Nursing & Rehabilitation Nineteenth Avenue 2017 (loss $1.0 million, paid $1.6 million); Kindred Transitional Care & Rehabilitation-Tunnell Center 2015 (loss $1.8 million, paid $6.2 million); Kindred Transitional Care and Rehabilitation-Lawton 2015 (loss $153,459, paid $3.9 million); Kindred Transitional Care and Rehabilitation-Tunnell Center 2016 (loss $889,836, paid $4.7 million); Lawton Skilled Nursing and Rehabilitation Center 2017 (loss $2.8 million, paid $3.8 million); Lawton Skilled Nursing and Rehabilitation Center 2018 (loss $644,087, paid $1.5 million); Lawton Skilled Nursing and Rehabilitation Center 2020 (loss $78,423, paid $2.2 million); San Francisco Health Care 2016 (loss $1.6 million, paid $5.2 million); Sequoias San Francisco Convalescent Hospital 2015 (loss $1.3 million, paid $2.1 million); Sequoias San Francisco Convalescent Hospital 2016 (loss $74,138, paid $2.2 million); Sequoias San Francisco Convalescent Hospital 2020 (loss $1.1 million, paid $2.4 million); Sheffield Convalescent Hospital 2015 (loss $324, paid $87,586).","how":"Report years 2015 to 2018 list related-party costs on page 3.1 (lines 10 to 34: account, related party, service, amount); 2020 on, page 10.4 (lines 30 to 99). Both are read with the same code as the case screen ltc-related-payments-sf. Negative entries are left out. The kind of payment is read from the account or cost centre and the description. Where a report names a person, the person is not shown.","limits":"Related-party dealings are permitted and these are the homes' own disclosures. Medi-Cal limits what a home may claim for a related purchase to the related company's own cost. A loss in a year with rent to the owner's property company is common where the rent was set under a long lease. The older form groups costs by income-statement account, so its kinds are coarser than page 10.4.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"home","t":"Nursing home","type":"org"},{"k":"party","t":"Related party","type":"org"},{"k":"kind","t":"Mostly for","type":"text"},{"k":"y2015","t":"2015","type":"usd"},{"k":"y2016","t":"2016","type":"usd"},{"k":"y2017","t":"2017","type":"usd"},{"k":"y2018","t":"2018","type":"usd"},{"k":"y2019","t":"2019","type":"usd"},{"k":"y2020","t":"2020","type":"usd"},{"k":"y2021","t":"2021","type":"usd"},{"k":"y2022","t":"2022","type":"usd"},{"k":"y2023","t":"2023","type":"usd"},{"k":"y2024","t":"2024","type":"usd"},{"k":"y2025","t":"2025","type":"usd"},{"k":"all","t":"All years","type":"usd"}],"rows":[{"home":"The Avenues Transitional Care Center","party":"Aspen Skilled Healthcare, Inc.","kind":"Management, home office and administration","y2015":null,"y2016":null,"y2017":null,"y2018":null,"y2019":936000,"y2020":7943624,"y2021":1167041,"y2022":1218607,"y2023":null,"y2024":null,"y2025":null,"all":1126527